      "message": "`bazel run` already works today. From the repo root:\n\n```\nbazel run //tools/formatter:formatter -- --check \u003cfile\u003e\n```\n\nresolves the relative path (via `BUILD_WORKING_DIRECTORY`) and defaults the\nprofile (via `BUILD_WORKSPACE_DIRECTORY`), so the explicit `--profile` in\n`tools/format-java` is redundant and no wrapper is actually required.\n\nSyntactic sugar: a root alias makes `bazel run format` work:\n\n```python\n# //BUILD\nalias(name \u003d \"format\", actual \u003d \"//tools/formatter:formatter\")\n```\n\n```\nbazel run format -- --check \u003cfile\u003e     # bare label, from repo root\nbazel run //:format -- --write \u003cfile\u003e  # from any directory\n```\n\nWorth documenting both forms here next to `tools/format-java`, and noting the bazel-run entry needs no shim. The shim\u0027s only advantage over the alias is cwd-independence: it locates the repo root itself.",
