      "side": 1,
      "message": "This whole file serves only `--changed-lines`. No established JDT-based\nformatter does changed-line scoping: revelc `formatter-maven-plugin`,\n`spring-javaformat`, `algodesigner/eclipse-format`, and the Eclipse headless\napp all format whole files. Dropping `--changed-lines` for v1 removes this\nfile entirely.\n\nIf it is re-added later, the whole file reduces to parsing\n`git diff --unified\u003d0 \u003cbase\u003e -- \u003cfile\u003e` hunk headers (`@@ -a,b +c,d @@`, where\n`+c,d` is the new-side changed range, count defaults to 1):\n\n```java\nrecord LineRange(int start, int count) {}\nvar ranges \u003d new ArrayList\u003cLineRange\u003e();\nvar hunk \u003d Pattern.compile(\"^@@ -\\\\d+(?:,\\\\d+)? \\\\+(\\\\d+)(?:,(\\\\d+))? @@\");\nfor (String line : runGit(\"diff\", \"--unified\u003d0\", base, \"--\", file)) {\n    var m \u003d hunk.matcher(line);\n    if (m.find()) {\n        int start \u003d Integer.parseInt(m.group(1));\n        int count \u003d m.group(2) \u003d\u003d null ? 1 : Integer.parseInt(m.group(2));\n        if (count \u003e 0) ranges.add(new LineRange(start, count));\n    }\n}\n```\n\nAn explicitly named new/untracked file is not shown by `git diff`; treat it as\nentirely changed, as the current code already does.",
